Z||000005||RossT||12-08-2000||04:30 AM||||Joe, you really need to look at it or have someone look at it for you.  T-top parts are very very hard to find. If the car is in good running shape, and all the t-top parts are in good working order, it is worth at least the min. bid.  I would never buy a fiero with out having a third party look at it. If the car is far away from you, you could find someone on PFF to check it out for you. I have had third parties look at cars for me and video tape it, then fed-ex the tape to me.<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||1
