Z||000007||Tom88gt||12-08-2000||11:11 AM||||I saw one on auction starting at $2000 once.  I bought my 88 Formula T-top of the internet site unseen ($3000 asking price).  I would not sell mine for less than $5000.  It all depends on what its worth to you and what its worth to the seller.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||12-08-2000||11:30 AM||||Don't bid too high on it 'cause it has a lot of milage.  Chances are it is going to need some suspension work done to it.  Maybe ball joints or brake work or other such items, which is not cheap on 88's.  However, if its in good working order I'd say it should be worth between the starting bid and $3500.  Although mine is not a t-top, I got my Formula in June 97 for $2850.  Although low on options, it has AC, and only had 67,000 miles!  The paint was mint on it and the interior was perfect except for cigarette burn holes in the drivers seat.  So don't go much higher, 'cause Formula's can be had for good prices!  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000009||AkursedX||12-08-2000||03:11 PM||||You should e-mail the bidder and ask him what the minor work needed to it is.  Most likely it is the above mentioned (brakes ball joints etc.) <BR> And if you don't live that far away, it would probably be worth your time to check it out.  It looks nice and of course it has T-tops, but the most i would bid would be about 3500 until I learned more about it.  <BR>Just my 2 cents  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
